title: "Beyond Like-for-Like: Linking Player Similarity with Post-Transfer Playing-Time Retention"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Rupayan"
    family-names: "Halder"
    affiliation: "Jadavpur University, Kolkata"
  - name: "ADDITIONAL AUTHOR(S), IF ANY, TO BE CONFIRMED"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RupayanHalder39/MITSloanProblem3-Player-Similarity-Transfer-Retention"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code, aggregate results and figures for a held-out evaluation of two separate football recruitment
  signals: behavioural player similarity retrieval and post-transfer playing-time retention. The two
  modules are evaluated independently and are not combined into a single recruitment score. Developed
  in collaboration with SoccerSolver. Underlying player and transfer data are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - football
  - soccer analytics
  - player similarity
  - transfer market
  - recruitment
  - held-out evaluation
